---
id: capellini-spezzati-with-light-cheddar
title: Capellini Spezzati with Light Cheddar
category: modular_carb

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 270

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: false

---

In a #saucepan, bring 1 liter of water to a rolling boil over high heat.

Add @capellini-spezzati{100%g} to the boiling water. Stir occasionally to keep the short strands separated and boil for ~boil-time{3.5%min} until al dente.

Drain in a fine-mesh colander, reserving 2 tbsp of the hot starchy pasta water.

Return the hot drained pasta to the warm pot off the heat. Immediately add @light-old-cheddar{50%g}, finely grated, and the 2 tbsp reserved pasta water. Stir vigorously for ~melt-time{25%sec} until the cheese melts into a smooth, creamy coating over the pasta.

Divide the cheesy pasta equally into 2 meal prep containers (135 g cooked yield each) and let cool before sealing.
